    "body": "Restore the original `constant_product::tokens_for_quote` call in the multi-hop buy path. The three physical source lines replace the local zero-quote guard and manual division while preserving the Truncation and BuyZeroAmount locations.\n\nThe actual current-source Linux control and candidate retain identical **1,019 normalized / 183 raw window memberships**. Aligned differing instruction slots decrease **3,423 \u2192 3,372**. The function size changes **18,056 \u2192 17,704 bytes** against original **18,584**, so its size gap increases; no complete function or whole-ELF match is claimed.\n\nThe restored 192-byte helper and both immediate callee bodies match the original under the unchanged narrow normalizer. The bounded reference audit also resolves all 590 data relocations and confirms identical control/candidate rodata. No recursive call closure or original whole-data identity is claimed.\n\nValidation: two actual normal source compilations; independent full source/build/census/runtime verification; 16 retained original/control/candidate triples with 48 verified signature records; finite resealed mutation controls and optimized-Python rejection; clean staged whitespace check. All retained candidate outcomes and ordered non-meter logs agree with original. Parent agrees too: **no runtime behavior gain is claimed**. The attempted zero-quote case stops at the earlier 6041 fee guard, so the helper's zero-quote and zero-denominator error paths remain unexercised.\n\nThe evidence packet explains the exact D037 workspace plus four maintained #1110 Rust changes used for the control, keeps the Cargo recipe unchanged, and distinguishes this Linux cohort from native macOS's 188 raw windows. SDK and frozen prior evidence are unchanged. Dedicated CI independently verifies the packet without recompiling or launching the VM.\n",
